## Context
Child of 1394. Stage 4 of the skill case notes pilot (`conception/2026-10-31-skill-case-notes.md` § 4); stage 2 (Claude read-back) passed headless in PR #2114. Pi's `idh-guard.ts` handles only `session_start` and `tool_call` today.

## Scope
Pi extension wiring on a read of `skills/<name>/SKILL.md`, calling `scripts/skill-case-notes.sh` (or its logic) with the same marker per context, and the same planted-token read-back.

## Exit criteria
- [ ] Pi read-back passes (token quoted, delivered once), or the reason it stopped is recorded on 1394

## Imagine (raid 1f0534)
- Premise holds: `adapters/pi/extensions/idh-guard.ts` handles session_start and tool_call only.
- Simplest path: in the extension, on a read tool call whose path ends `skills/<name>/SKILL.md`, call `scripts/skill-case-notes.sh` with a synthesized payload and inject its additionalContext through the extension API; probe first that an injected message reaches the model (`pi --print </dev/null`).
- Shares `scripts/skill-case-notes.sh` with 1404: additive changes only.

## Feasibility (raid 1f0534)
- PASS. idh-guard.ts:61,87. A `tool_result` handler appending the note to the read result may be simpler than injecting from `tool_call`. Live file is symlinked into the checkout: a merge changes the host.
- Record results on this ticket only; the orchestrator copies them to 1394.
